STAAD PLANE  COVERED ENTRY STAIRWELL - TRANSVERSE FRAME, 1 m STRIP
*
* ==========================================================================
*  COVERED ENTRY STAIRWELL - UNDERGROUND CBRN SHELTER, PUNE   REV F + MOD M1
*  MOD M1 shifts the stairwell +200 in X (9250-16050).  This is a TRANSVERSE 1 m
*  strip, so the shift does not change any dimension in this model.
*
*  WHY THIS STRUCTURE EXISTS
*  The Rev E approach was an OPEN cut 4.800 x 1.500, 2.000 deep, with the
*  outer door at its foot.  Three faults, all fixed by roofing it:
*    (a) no gravity outfall - every drop of rain had to be pumped, so a
*        pump failure flooded the only entrance;
*    (b) the entrance sat at the bottom of a permanent sump, which is where
*        dense CBRN agents collect - the worst possible place for the door
*        of a CBRN shelter;
*    (c) it could not simply be lidded at grade: the headroom at the top of
*        the steps would have been ZERO.
*  Rev F roofs the stair and moves the external door to GRADE at the head
*  of the stair, with the ground falling away from it.
*
*  THIS MODEL is the transverse box frame at the platform end, where the
*  walls retain the most.  A 1 m strip, PLANE frame.  The stair, the
*  headhouse and the shelter below are NOT in this model and do not change.
*
*  clear width 1.500   walls 250   floor 250   roof 250
*
*  ROOF / PLATFORM JUNCTION.  The roof is kept at 250 here.  Master B.6 designs the
*  stairwell raking roof as 250 (T12 @ 200 EF EW), Master A.7.6 loads a 250 roof and
*  Master F.2 registers it as 250; the 500 roof of Master B.7.1 is the HEADHOUSE roof,
*  a 396.5 kN/m2 blast element on a different footprint (headhouse Y 200-6000, platform
*  Y 6000-7500).  The 250 stairwell roof therefore runs to the headhouse wall face and
*  the 500 headhouse roof starts there.  The clause in Master A.4.7 that reads "over the
*  platform it becomes the 500 headhouse roof" is the only text that reads otherwise and
*  has NOT been changed - see the handover note.
*  floor -2.000   roof soffit +0.400   berm crest +0.900  (Master A.4.6 / A.4.7)
*  wall span (c/c) 2.650   roof span (c/c) 1.750
*  M35 / Fe500D,  Ec = 29.580 x 10^6 kN/m2   (Master A.5 - shelter/stairs/headhouse)
*  Was M30 in the as-received model; corrected to M35 so that the Ld = 40 phi
*  (T16 -> 640) already detailed in Master B.6 / F.2 is valid.  In M30 the same
*  bar needs 46 phi = 736 and every stairwell lap would be 13 % short.
*
*  SOIL
*   engineered fill  gamma = 20.0 kN/m3,  phi = 30 deg   (Master A.6 bulk unit weight)
*   at rest  K0 = 1 - sin(phi) = 0.50   (propped wall, so at-rest and
*   not active - the roof props the head and the floor props the foot)
*   construction surcharge 10.0 kPa -> K0 x q = 5.0 kPa
*   earth over the roof 0.300 m -> 5.40 kN/m2
*   subgrade modulus 100000 kN/m3, as adopted for the shelter mat
*
*  Units: metre, kilonewton.  X across the stairwell, Y up.
* ==========================================================================
*
START JOB INFORMATION
ENGINEER DATE 25-Aug-2026
JOB NAME ENTRY STAIRWELL - REV F + MOD M1
END JOB INFORMATION
*
INPUT WIDTH 79
UNIT METER KN
JOINT COORDINATES
1 0.0000 -2.1250 0.0;
2 0.2917 -2.1250 0.0;
3 0.5833 -2.1250 0.0;
4 0.8750 -2.1250 0.0;
5 1.1667 -2.1250 0.0;
6 1.4583 -2.1250 0.0;
7 1.7500 -2.1250 0.0;
8 0.0000 -1.4625 0.0;
9 0.0000 -0.8000 0.0;
10 0.0000 -0.1375 0.0;
11 0.0000 0.5250 0.0;
12 1.7500 -1.4625 0.0;
13 1.7500 -0.8000 0.0;
14 1.7500 -0.1375 0.0;
15 1.7500 0.5250 0.0;
16 0.2917 0.5250 0.0;
17 0.5833 0.5250 0.0;
18 0.8750 0.5250 0.0;
19 1.1667 0.5250 0.0;
20 1.4583 0.5250 0.0;
