*
START GROUP DEFINITION
MEMBER
_FLOOR 1 TO 6
_WALL_S 7 TO 10
_WALL_N 11 TO 14
_ROOF 15 TO 20
END GROUP DEFINITION
*
DEFINE MATERIAL START
ISOTROPIC M35
E 29580398
POISSON 0.2
DENSITY 25.0
ALPHA 1e-05
DAMP 0.05
TYPE CONCRETE
STRENGTH FCU 35000
END DEFINE MATERIAL
*
MEMBER PROPERTY
* 1 m strip: ZD = 1.000, YD = the element thickness
1 TO 6 PRIS YD 0.250 ZD 1.000
7 TO 14 PRIS YD 0.250 ZD 1.000
15 TO 20 PRIS YD 0.250 ZD 1.000
*
CONSTANTS
MATERIAL M35 ALL
*
SUPPORTS
* floor on elastic foundation: a vertical spring at each floor joint,
* k = subgrade x tributary length x 1 m strip.  FX released at one joint
* only, to restrain the frame horizontally without inventing a prop.
2 FIXED BUT FX MZ KFY 29167
3 FIXED BUT FX MZ KFY 29167
4 FIXED BUT FX MZ KFY 29167
5 FIXED BUT FX MZ KFY 29167
6 FIXED BUT FX MZ KFY 29167
7 FIXED BUT FX MZ KFY 14583
* one joint also holds FX - it stands for base friction and passive
* resistance on the floor slab, which are not modelled explicitly
1 FIXED BUT MZ KFY 14583
*
* ============================ LOADING =====================================
LOAD 1 LOADTYPE Dead TITLE DL SELFWEIGHT PLUS EARTH OVER THE ROOF
SELFWEIGHT Y -1.0
MEMBER LOAD
* Roof build-up, Master A.7.6 / B.6:  self 6.25 (SELFWEIGHT) + wp/screed 2.0
* + earth lap 5.4 + imposed 20.0 = 33.65 kN/m2  ->  wu = 1.5 x 33.65 = 50.5 kN/m2.
* The 5.4 earth lap is the Master's stated value; it slightly exceeds the 5.0 that a
* 250 lap at gamma 20 would give, and is kept because the Master establishes it.
15 TO 20 UNI GY -5.400
* waterproofing and protection screed
15 TO 20 UNI GY -2.000
*
LOAD 2 LOADTYPE Live TITLE LL 20.0 kN/m2 ON THE BERM OVER THE ROOF
MEMBER LOAD
* Master A.7.6 / B.6: 20 kN/m2 imposed, taken deliberately for a stray vehicle on
* the berm.  Was 1.5 (accessible-roof value) in the as-received model.
15 TO 20 UNI GY -20.000
*
LOAD 3 LOADTYPE Soil TITLE EARTH AT REST BOTH WALLS
MEMBER LOAD
* TRAP values computed PER MEMBER - STAAD's TRAP has no datum, so one
* trapezoid per wall would give a sawtooth that the statics check misses.
* sigma_h = K0 . gamma . (0.900 - y) = 0.50 x 20.0 x (0.900 - y) = 10.0 (0.900 - y)
* At the platform level -2.000 this gives 29.0 kN/m2, which with the 5.0 kN/m2
* surcharge of LOAD 4 reproduces the 34 kN/m2 at base stated in Master B.6.
7 TRAP GX 30.2500 23.6250
8 TRAP GX 23.6250 17.0000
9 TRAP GX 17.0000 10.3750
10 TRAP GX 10.3750 3.7500
11 TRAP GX -30.2500 -23.6250
12 TRAP GX -23.6250 -17.0000
13 TRAP GX -17.0000 -10.3750
14 TRAP GX -10.3750 -3.7500
*
LOAD 4 LOADTYPE Soil TITLE SURCHARGE 10 kPa AT REST BOTH WALLS
MEMBER LOAD
7 TO 10 UNI GX 5.0000
11 TO 14 UNI GX -5.0000
*
LOAD 5 LOADTYPE Soil TITLE EARTH ONE SIDE ONLY - BACKFILLING CASE
MEMBER LOAD
7 TRAP GX 30.2500 23.6250
8 TRAP GX 23.6250 17.0000
9 TRAP GX 17.0000 10.3750
10 TRAP GX 10.3750 3.7500
*
* ---- IS 456 : 2000 Cl 36.4.1 and Table 18 -------------------------------
LOAD COMB 101 1.5 DL + 1.5 LL + 1.5 EARTH + 1.5 SURCHARGE
1 1.5 2 1.5 3 1.5 4 1.5
LOAD COMB 102 1.5 DL + 1.5 EARTH + 1.5 SURCHARGE  NO ROOF LL
1 1.5 3 1.5 4 1.5
LOAD COMB 103 0.9 DL + 1.5 EARTH + 1.5 SURCHARGE  MINIMUM RESTRAINT
1 0.9 3 1.5 4 1.5
LOAD COMB 104 1.5 DL + 1.5 EARTH ONE SIDE  CONSTRUCTION
1 1.5 5 1.5
LOAD COMB 201 1.0 DL + 1.0 LL + 1.0 EARTH + 1.0 SURCHARGE  SERVICE
1 1.0 2 1.0 3 1.0 4 1.0
*
PERFORM ANALYSIS PRINT STATICS CHECK
*
PRINT SUPPORT REACTION ALL
PRINT MEMBER FORCES ALL
FINISH
